	(text "ADS1115 on ISO_3V3, I2C address 0x48 (JP 1-2, default) or 0x49 (2-3). ALERT/RDY unused.\nAll channels are read single-ended (aquaPi driver): AIN0 on-board pH, AIN1 pH reference\n(monitor, allows AIN0-AIN1 differential later), AIN2 external pH amplifier module, AIN3 general."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 184.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2420f22a-5685-45e5-89db-b60bc300d2ee")
	)
	(text "ISO1540: side 2 (normal low level) on the Pi I2C bus; side 1 (low level 0.57..0.8 V) only drives the\nADS1115 (V_IL 0.99 V at 3.3 V). Side-1 pull-ups 4k7 -> 0.7 mA, within the required 0.5..3.5 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 176.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4671adee-5393-4042-ace7-c0c117640656")
	)
	(text "AIN3: general 0..3.3 V input on the isolated side (sensor GND must be ISO_GND!), 1k + 100n,\nclamped. Terminal: ISO_3V3 / AIN3 / ISO_GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 422.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6aa60616-c2aa-4b93-b32e-e2156d0ce2f8")
	)
	(text "AIN2: external pH amplifier module (probe kit board), terminal ISO_5V / SIG / ISO_GND - isolated\nas well. Output (about 2.5 V at pH 7) filtered 10k/10u (1.6 Hz) and clamped to 0..3.3 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 375.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8600735c-7f21-40b2-a2ce-a3e841a6e264")
	)
	(text "TL431B (TI, DBZ pinout 1=K 2=REF 3=A; TL432 differs!), ~1.6 mA via 470R. Divided and buffered\nto PH_REF = 1.25 V, which also drives the probe reference electrode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 368.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "94cd84fc-20af-466a-986e-3f5d43af7563")
	)
	(text "Probe load: TLV9062 input (0.5 pA typ) and the polystyrene (styroflex) filter cap across the probe;\nno ceramic cap or clamp on PH_BNC/PH_IN (leakage). Cap x electrode R (100M..1G): 0.2..2 s input filter;\nswap for 47p..6n8 as needed. Second 50 Hz filter after the buffer: 10k/10u, 1.6 Hz.\nLAYOUT: guard ring around PH_BNC, R/C input parts and TLV9062 pin 3, connected to PH_BUF; slots; clean flux."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 307.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a8f7b78c-186f-488d-bad6-d6c53b17246c")
	)
	(text "On-board pH front end: glass electrode on BNC centre, reference on BNC shell. The probe is\nbiased to PH_REF = 1.25 V (TL431 2.495 V / 2), so AIN0 reads 1.25 V +/- 59 mV/pH single-ended;\naquaPi's 2-point calibration removes the offset. BNC shell pads must stay on PH_REF, NOT GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 254 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aa31099b-78b4-4126-a010-c31e95775e46")
	)
	(text "1W isolated DC/DC, 1 kV. 1k dummy load (5 mA) plus LDO quiescent current keep its output from\nrising at light load. ISO_5V also supplies the external pH module terminal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dc15fbc8-9955-4970-af32-72761523a059")
	)
	(text "The whole analog section is galvanically isolated (ISO_GND). The tank water is often tied to\nboard GND through other sensors (e.g. a DS18B20 sleeve); without isolation a DC current would flow\nthrough the pH reference electrode and destroy it. LAYOUT: keep >= 2 mm (better a slot) between the\nGND and ISO_GND domains; only the B0505S DC/DC and the ISO1540 cross the gap."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "de604a7b-29c3-4304-8471-cc682a724d43")
	)
